**Naming Evaluation**:
- `processScenario`: still appropriate
- `componentCounts`: clear
- `COMPONENT_TYPES`, `COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE`, `COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM`: all clear and intent-revealing
- Decision: Keep all names

**Current Code**:
```typescript
const COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set(["rune", "moonstone"]);
const COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;
const COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;

export function processScenario(input: any): ScenarioResult {
  const results = input.steps.map((step: any) => {
    let basePremium = 0;
    const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};
    for (const item of step.items) {
      if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {
        componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;
      } else {
        basePremium += BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;
      }
    }
    for (const [type, count] of Object.entries(componentCounts)) {
      if (count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE) {
        basePremium += COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;
      } else {
        basePremium += count * (BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0);
      }
    }
    return { premium: basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE };
  });
  return { results };
}
```

The quote logic inside the `map` callback is getting complex. I can extract a `calculateQuotePremium` function to improve Rule 2 (reveals intent) and reduce the cognitive load of the main function.

